  "live_records": {
    "q-57957": {
      "dom_id": "step-q57957",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "If $\\frac{4}{3}x=8$, then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}x & =8 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}x & =8\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\cancel{3}}x & =8\\cdot 3 \\\\ 4x & =24\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $4$ to isolate $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}4x & =24 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}x}{\\cancel{4}} & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
